{
  "requirement": "In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to stop after the requirements commit.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. In a design session with no code to write, the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to stop after the requirements commit.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_stops_after_the_commit_in_a_design_session]` covers it. It finds the workflow step of `habeas-requirements` that contains \"all groups together\", which is the commit step. It then calls `assert_text_in_order` on that step's text. The helper panics unless \"then commit it\" appears first and \"In a design session with no code to write, stop here\" appears after it.\n\nThese assertions enforce both parts of the clause: the design-session condition and the stop instruction, placed after the commit. A skill without the stop sentence, or one that put it before the commit instruction, would fail. The helpers `step`, `step_of` and `assert_text_in_order` are reached from the marked test, so they need no markers of their own.\n\nThe requirement names no other modes or boundaries. I found no gaps.",
